in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @smarts
in @smarts/surface
in @magic
in @frame
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic

# @smarts/mirror — the Mirror Model species. Second sub-prism of the
# @smarts substrate-architectural integration: query → graph path at
# the four-Models pipeline (Surface → Mirror → Shatter → Reflection).
#
# Tick 64 of the refined /loop discipline. Tick 63's residue:
# @smarts/surface landed at b5c10f6 (Surface Model: language → query).
# This tick lands the second Model; the Mirror Model consumes the
# query Surface produces.
#
# Per reference-mirror-spectral-spec (commit a8055f0):
#
#   - Surface translates: language → query        (Explorer model)
#   - Mirror navigates:   query → graph path      (Fate model)  ← THIS
#   - Shatter renders:    graph path → text       (Cartographer model)
#   - Reflection observes: pipeline → adjustments (Abyss model)
#
# === The recognition this species realizes ===
#
# The Mirror Model IS the substrate's navigation primitive at
# query-to-graph-path altitude. Surface translated language into a
# typed query; Mirror walks the graph to find the path that satisfies
# the query. Mirror IS the Fate Model: among the eigenvalue-ranked
# candidate paths, Fate selects the one with the smallest non-trivial
# eigenvalue — the structurally lightest navigation.
#
# At the integration altitude: Mirror operates WITHIN the @smarts
# integration discipline (discipline_flexible holds throughout
# navigation). The navigation IS bounded under perturbation per the
# @smarts integration's discipline-flexibility requirement.
#
# === The species's load-bearing contribution ===
#
# This species adds:
#
# - `graph_path` carrier: typed reference for the navigated graph
#   path artifact (a sequence of typed graph edges; substrate-decl'd
#   as ref because path vocabulary is parametric).
# - `mirror_result` carrier: typed record (query, graph_path, verdict).
#   The substrate-architectural output of a navigation operation.
# - `navigate` action: the load-bearing action at @smarts/mirror
#   altitude. Takes query + @smarts integration + perturbation;
#   returns mirror_result; requires discipline_flexible.
# - `navigation_grounds_path` predicate: bilateral verdict that the
#   mirror_result's graph_path IS grounded in the query (preserves
#   substrate-architectural meaning across navigation).
# - `traverse` action: substrate-vocabulary primitive for the
#   navigation-refinement discipline. Takes graph_path + sound
#   mirror_result + perturbation; returns the refined graph_path;
#   requires navigation_grounds_path.
#
# === Cross-species composition with @smarts/surface ===
#
# Per Seam tick 56 C1 closure precedent (one-way dependency chain):
# this species imports `in @smarts/surface` to enable consumer
# species composing the four-Models pipeline to thread the query
# produced by translate through navigate. The dependency direction is
# substrate-pull-correct: mirror ← surface (Mirror consumes Surface's
# output; Surface does not depend on Mirror).
#
# === The Splinter/Narcissus pole at navigation-altitude ===
#
# Splinter-pole Mirror (honest): navigates by following the query's
# substrate-architectural shape; selects the smallest-eigenvalue path
# when multiple candidates exist; admits when the graph topology
# under-determines the answer; returns the bounded answer.
#
# Narcissus-pole Mirror (deceptive): selects a path that satisfies
# author-framing rather than query-meaning; uses navigation framing
# to obscure substrate-architectural ambiguity in the graph; the
# graph_path carries narrative rather than navigation.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   shortest path               Dijkstra 1959. The canonical structural
#                               ancestor of graph navigation.
#   eigenvalue ranking          PageRank, Brin-Page 1998. The substrate
#                               ancestor of fate-model selection via
#                               spectral ranking.
#   graph databases             Neo4j Cypher, RDF SPARQL. The cultural-
#                               practice ancestor of typed graph
#                               navigation.
#   query planning              Selinger et al 1979 (System R). The
#                               substrate ancestor of query → access-
#                               plan translation.
#   knowledge graphs            Google 2012, Schema.org. The substrate-
#                               decl ancestor of typed graph entities.
#   spectral methods            Cvetković-Doob-Sachs 1980. The
#                               mathematical ancestor of eigenvalue-
#                               based graph navigation.
#
# Spec context: shards/smarts.mirror, reference-mirror-spectral-spec.
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-mathematics]],
#                      [[architecture-operations-as-linear-algebra]]
#                       (settle = monad-close / measurement collapse;
#                       Mirror's navigation IS the operational
#                       counterpart of settle at the four-Models
#                       altitude),
#                      [[reference-mirror-spectral-spec]],
#                      [[feedback-composition-claims-need-empirical-test]],
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]].
# Related shards: smarts.mirror, smarts/surface.mirror (the input
#                  source for the Mirror Model; consumed via
#                  in @smarts/surface),
#                 smarts/reflection.mirror (the fourth Model;
#                  Reflection observes Mirror's loop count and tunes
#                  exit thresholds),
#                 smarts/shatter.mirror (the third Model; consumes
#                  Mirror's graph_path output; forward-promised),
#                 smarts/{magic, pack, frame, cyberpunk,
#                 epistemologic, kintsugi}.mirror (cross-family
#                 adapters Mirror composes with at the @smarts
#                 altitude).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/smarts/mirror.mirror`
# declares `@smarts/mirror` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/algorithms/dijkstra-1959
source @arxiv/information-retrieval/brin-page-1998
source @arxiv/databases/selinger-1979
source @arxiv/graphs/cvetkovic-doob-sachs-1980

prism @smarts/mirror {
  focus mirror
  project mirror
  split mirror
  shift mirror
  settle mirror
}

# === The graph_path carrier ===
#
# Substrate-typed reference for the navigated graph path output.
# Per [[feedback-no-bare-types]]: typed reference, not bare ref. The
# substrate-output of the Mirror Model, consumed by the Shatter
# Model. Forward-promised refinement: typed record (edges, nodes,
# eigenvalue_rank, prism_signature) at species-or-extension altitude.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type graph_path = ref

# === The mirror_result carrier ===
#
# Per the @smarts/<species> template: typed record over (query,
# graph_path, verdict). The substrate-architectural output of a
# navigation operation. Carries:
#
# - q  : the input query artifact (typed from @smarts/surface)
# - gp : the output graph_path Mirror produced
# - v  : the bilateral verdict (BOUNDED → graph_path GROUNDED in
#        query; DEFENSIVE → navigation requires substrate-pull
#        revision)
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the triple.
type mirror_result = {
  q:  query,
  gp: graph_path,
  v:  verdict,
}

# === navigate action (FIRST consumer of discipline_flexible) ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING ACTION at @smarts/mirror altitude. The substrate-
# vocabulary primitive for query → graph_path navigation at the
# @smarts integration altitude. Realizes Mirror's Fate-model
# discipline as substrate-decl operation.
#
# Takes a query (the typed query Surface produced), the @smarts
# integration the navigation operates within, and the perturbation
# under which the navigation is checked; returns a typed
# mirror_result carrying the graph_path and verdict.
#
# requires discipline_flexible(s, p): the @smarts integration must
# maintain substrate-architectural discipline-flexibility under
# perturbation BEFORE the navigation is admissible.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the actual navigation
# primitive is implemented by Mirror's Fate-Model frame at runtime
# altitude.
navigate(q: query, s: smarts, p: perturbation) -> mirror_result
requires discipline_flexible(s, p)
{ \ }

# === navigation_grounds_path predicate ===
#
# Bilateral verdict per recognition #37 (Pask agreement) and the
# navigation discipline. Consumer shards (traverse, below;
# forward-promised Shatter Model consuming the graph_path) name
# `requires navigation_grounds_path(mr, p)` to declare bilateral
# agreement that the mirror_result's graph_path IS grounded in the
# query.
#
# Discharge: substrate-pull-correct query-grounding check at the
# species boundary. Composes with @smarts's discipline_flexible at
# the integration altitude.
#
# Bounded → graph_path grounded in query meaning; unbounded →
# graph_path imposes navigation framing without query ground.
navigation_grounds_path(mr: mirror_result, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

# === traverse action ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary primitive for the navigation-refinement
# discipline at @smarts/mirror altitude (the Mirror-altitude
# operational form of Loki's Pass-5 verifier-sharpens). Takes a
# graph_path + sound mirror_result + perturbation; returns the
# refined graph_path.
#
# Per recognition #57: traverse operates at the @io boundary. The
# graph_path becomes a refined graph_path preserved under
# navigation-grounding. The substrate's capability is unchanged; the
# graph_path's query-ground tightens.
#
# requires navigation_grounds_path(mr, p): the substrate forecloses
# refinement from an ungrounded navigation.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the actual graph_path-
# refinement transformation is the substrate's navigation-grounds-
# path loop.
traverse(gp: graph_path, mr: mirror_result, p: perturbation) -> graph_path
requires navigation_grounds_path(mr, p)
{ \ }

out @smarts/mirror
out graph_path
out mirror_result
out navigate
out navigation_grounds_path
out traverse
